1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,780
If you descend from people who were enslaved, you descend from people who at some point in history, their liberation, their freedom was relegated to their interior life.

2
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:12,360
They didn't have agency in their bodies.

3
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:17,180
My great-great-great-grandmother didn't have agency over what she ate, what she did.

4
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:26,060
She didn't always have full agency over what she said, but what she did have agency over are those secret places, I believe, in her inner world that no master can touch.

5
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:29,000
I like to think they were cussing out people in their minds.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:36,520
Also, preserving stories, preserving memory in their interior lives that they weren't always able to articulate in the world around them.

7
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:43,840
And so the journey for us to stay close to, you know, the Black interior, it's an intergenerational calling.

8
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:46,140
It's an intergenerational way of being in the world.

